WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:10.420
FedRAMP Moderate is one of the most commonly discussed FedRAMP baselines because many federal cloud use cases involve information and operations where a security incident could create serious consequences.

2
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:19.960
At a high level, FedRAMP provides a standardized federal approach for security assessment, authorization support, and continuous monitoring of cloud services.

3
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:26.140
Moderate is the baseline used when the cloud service offering supports a moderate-impact federal use case.

4
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.060
Moderate is not a product quality label.

5
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:35.960
It does not mean the service is better than a Low-impact service or less professional than a High-impact service.

6
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:41.100
It means the security expectations are aligned to a particular level of federal risk.

7
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:47.680
A provider can have a well-engineered Low service, a poorly operated Moderate service, or a mature High service.

8
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:53.940
The baseline only becomes meaningful when it is implemented, tested, monitored, and maintained.

9
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.780
Several concepts are easy to confuse.

10
00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.680
The baseline is the set of control expectations.

11
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.860
The cloud service offering is the specific service boundary being assessed.

12
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.960
The authorization package is the evidence and documentation describing how the service meets expectations.

13
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:15.420
The agency risk decision is made by an authorizing official or appropriate agency authority.

14
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.800
Actual security operation is the daily work that keeps the service protected after the package is assembled.

15
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.960
The practical takeaway is that FedRAMP Moderate is common, but it is still demanding.

16
00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:35.100
It requires real engineering, clear scope, disciplined operations, accurate documentation, assessment evidence, and ongoing monitoring.

17
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.120
A Moderate baseline does not guarantee security by itself.

18
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:46.820
It gives stakeholders a structured way to evaluate whether the service is appropriately protected for a moderate-impact federal use case.
